  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Movement verbs and reference point",
     "texto": [
      "The verbs **ra, vào, lên, xuống, về, sang/qua** can specify direction or the relation to a reference point; they're not chosen just by looking at a map.",
      "**Ra** usually expresses movement outwards or towards an open space; **vào**, inwards. On trips around Vietnam, **ra Bắc/ra Hà Nội** and **vào Nam/vào Sài Gòn** are also common. This north-south axis is a usage convention: interpret the sentence from its context and the speaker's point of view.",
      "**Lên/xuống** usually mark movement up or down: «lên núi» (go up the mountain), «xuống tầng dưới» (go down to the floor below). They don't automatically mean going to a more \"important\" place or to the coast.",
      "**Về** means returning home or to one's own place; **sang/qua** means crossing to the other side or to another place: «về quê», «sang Lào», «qua sông»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Behind another verb, they mark the direction",
     "texto": [
      "These same words attach after a movement verb: **chạy ra** (run out), **bước vào** (walk in), **leo lên** (climb up), **nhìn xuống** (look down), **mang về** (take home), **gửi sang** (send across).",
      "If there's an object, it goes **in the middle**: «mang **hành lý** lên phòng» = take the luggage up to the room."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
